Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.10 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008) with glibc 2.28 and no IPv6.
q2-filebrowser runs from the card's .filebrowser folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's
patch/addon.c): Q2 Pod lists it in Streaming, turns it on from that row and shows its QR code, draws
its page and keeps the Q2 awake while files move. Nothing is flashed for it.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.filebrowser, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-filebrowser-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP
  launcher.sh  installed as .filebrowser/run: q2-filebrowser copied to /tmp and run there in a
               restart loop
  q2app        installed as .filebrowser/q2app: the card app manifest (name=File Browser, qr=1: its
               row opens the QR code page once it answers)
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app

Install
-------

Q2 Pod's System settings -> Apps installs the latest release over Wi-Fi. By hand, unzip
q2-filebrowser-*.zip from https://github.com/group-a-study/q2-filebrowser/releases/latest to the
card's root with the Q2 powered off. See the top-level README.md.

Build
-----

  contrib/shanlingq2/build.sh [OUT]

Go 1.22 or later and python3; nothing outside Go's standard library. The binary is CGO_ENABLED=0
GOOS=linux GOARCH=mipsle GOMIPS=softfloat, static, so it needs none of the Q2's libraries. Tests
(go test ./...): the key and PIN made once and kept, signing in by either, the PIN's lockout, X-Q2
on a change; listing (folders first, dot files only when asked, .. kept inside the card), search; a
download whole and by range, its sandbox, an HTML file as bytes; a ZIP of a folder and a file,
stored, without dot files, and its name; making a folder, uploads (a folder's paths kept, a taken
name numbered or replaced, a name that tries to climb out, past one chunk, no .q2part left),
renaming (a case change on FAT, a taken name, a bad one), moving (numbered where taken, not into
itself), deleting (all or none), Read Only, the card away; the Q2's page, what is moving, the hold,
Turn Off; and stopping by itself, though not during a transfer. python3
contrib/shanlingq2/test_launcher.py tests the launcher. A tag q2-vX.Y matching
cmd/q2-filebrowser/main.go's version publishes the release (.github/workflows/release.yml).

Device
------

Q2 Pod runs /bin/sh /mnt/mmc/.filebrowser/run when Streaming's File Browser row is pressed and it
isn't running. The launcher copies q2-filebrowser and itself to /tmp and leaves the card at once; the
loop restarts it after a crash, waiting 5 s and doubling to a minute, and leaves its pid in
/tmp/q2-filebrowser. An exit of 0 (turned off from the Q2, or idle for idle_minutes) ends the loop.
A TERM to it stops q2-filebrowser cleanly, an upload under way dropped: Q2 Pod sends it for Stop
Streaming Services, Home's Rockbox row, an Apps update or remove, and USB storage (after which it
starts it again; meanwhile the page says the card is away).

Uploads are written aside, as a hidden .<name>.q2part beside where they go, in 512 KB chunks, each
opened, written, synced and closed, so the card is almost never busy; the whole file is renamed into
place once it is all there (and of the length the browser said), and a broken upload leaves nothing.

  /tmp/q2-filebrowser.state
      addr (the page's, with its port), pin, qr and qrsize (the code for the address with the key),
      note, hold (1: keep the Q2 awake), version
  /tmp/q2-filebrowser.sock
      the datagram q stops it
  /tmp/q2-filebrowser.browse.sock
      Q2SPOT/1 (q2-pod's docs/librespot.md) for the Q2's page: menu (remote Open on Your Phone, an
      info row, action readonly and action stop, asked again every 2 s), and the actions readonly
      and stop
  port 8000 (the next free one if taken)
      the page and its API, behind the cookie: GET /api/state (version, read only, free and total
      bytes, the card there), GET /api/list?path=&hidden=, GET /api/search?path=&q=&hidden=,
      GET /api/file?path=&inline= (ranges), GET /api/zip?path=..., PUT
      /api/upload?dir=&name=&overwrite= (the body is the file), and POST /api/mkdir, /api/rename,
      /api/move, /api/delete with JSON (path, name, paths, to). POST /api/login takes the PIN;
      /?k=KEY sets the cookie. Errors are JSON {"error": "..."} with the HTTP status: 403 read only,
      404 not there, 409 a name taken, 503 the card away, 507 no room
  .filebrowser/config.json
      web_key and pin (delete them for new ones), read_only, and idle_minutes (0: never off by
      itself); updates keep it
